Apple's new iPhone 18 Pro and iPhone 18 Pro Max began arriving to customers on Friday, and unfortunately some early adopters are experiencing Face ID issues.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/Face-ID-iPhone-18-Pro.jpg" alt="" width="1672" height="941" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1066479" /><br/>
According to a <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/iphone18pro/s/PWuX4lKgoe">Reddit post</a> spotted <a href="https://9to5mac.com/2026/09/21/iphone-18-pro-face-id-bug-system-reboot/">by <em>9to5Mac</em></a>, Face ID authentication for specific actions such as unlocking a locked app sometimes fails to work on the iPhone 18 Pro models, and the device then freezes and eventually reboots to the lock screen. It is unclear how widespread this problem is, but it can be hit or miss and not all users are affected.<br/>
<br/>
In addition, some <em>MacRumors</em> forum members are experiencing other Face ID issues on the iPhone 18 Pro models. First, some are <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/new-18-pro-face-id-not-available.2489810/">receiving a "Face ID is Not Available" message</a> when attempting to set up Face ID, and others have noted that the devices <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/iphone-18-pro-unlocks-even-if-im-not-looking-directly-at-it.2489950/">do not always seem to be respecting the "Require Attention for Face ID" setting</a> when it is enabled.<br/>
<br/>
